Check for and install updates

Runs the bundled `snouty-update` helper, which checks for a newer release and
replaces the snouty binary in place. Does nothing if `snouty-update` is not
installed alongside snouty.

Pass a version to install a specific release instead of the latest, including
pre-releases:
  snouty update 0.6.0
  snouty update 0.6.0-rc.1

The update channel decides what "latest" means: `stable` (the default) installs
the latest release, `unstable` also considers pre-releases but still installs
the latest release when it is newer than every pre-release. Set the channel with
the `update_channel` setting (or SNOUTY_UPDATE_CHANNEL), and override it for one
run with --channel:
  snouty update --channel unstable

Installing a version older than the one you're running is a downgrade and
requires --force.

Usage: snouty update [OPTIONS] [VERSION]

Arguments:
  [VERSION]
          Release to install (e.g. 0.6.0 or 0.6.0-rc.1). Defaults to the latest
          release

Options:
      --force
          Install the requested version even if it is older than the current one
          (a downgrade)

      --channel <CHANNEL>
          Update channel to use, overriding the `update_channel` setting

          Possible values:
          - stable:   Install the latest release
          - unstable: Also consider pre-releases, but prefer the latest release
            when it is newer

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
